<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Cultel yr shr, div edge higher.</title>
<headline>Cultel yr shr, div edge higher.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     10.5	  vs    10.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  5.25	 vs     5.00</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    1.82	 vs     1.79</p>
<p>    Retained income	  6.48	 vs     5.57</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    3.71	 vs     3.47</p>
<p>    Tax			  1.44	 vs     1.52</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    0.17	 vs     0.17</p>
<p>    Turnover		  31.25	 vs    27.69</p>
<p>Full name: Cullinan Hotel and Leisure Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Cultel was previously known as Concorde Travel Holdings. It changed its name to Cultel in January following a reverse listing.</p>
<p>The company said market research indicated an above-average sustainable growth rate in the medium to long term in the tourism, travel and related South African industries.</p>
<p>Expansion of the hotel group would be focused in the select services market, it said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
